#
# objcopy --redefine-syms input, RV64IMAC's own, applied to the archives holding kernel text
# ON TOP OF cmake/kernel_runtime.syms (kickos_privatise_runtime in cmake/kickos.cmake).
#
# rv64imac names no bit-manipulation extension, so the compiler lowers __builtin_clzll and
# __builtin_ctzll to libgcc calls (kernel/sched/policy_fifo_rr.cc, kernel/mem/frame.cc).
# Where the image is split, libgcc is linked into the APP's half and out of the kernel's
# reach, so the kernel links its own (arch/riscv/rv64imac/libgcc_rv64imac.cc).
#
# Under private names: a kernel-side definition of `__clzdi2` is the definition the whole
# link sees, so an APP-side libgcc member needing it resolves across the halves and the
# link fails.
#
# Both spellings, as the fleet-wide map carries: objcopy ignores an entry matching no
# symbol.
__clzdi2 kickos_rv64_clzdi2
__ctzdi2 kickos_rv64_ctzdi2
___clzdi2 _kickos_rv64_clzdi2
___ctzdi2 _kickos_rv64_ctzdi2
